{"id":"mahabharata-6-009","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":9,"title":"नवमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 9 · The varshas and their peoples","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya names the varshas such as Ramanaka, Hairanyavata and Harivarsha with their mountains and inhabitants. He ends with Narayana, called Vaikuntha by the gods and Vishnu by the Vedas.","kn":"ರಮಣಕ, ಹೈರಣ್ಯವತ, ಹರಿವರ್ಷ ಮೊದಲಾದ ವರ್ಷಗಳನ್ನು ಅವುಗಳ ಪರ್ವತಗಳು, ನಿವಾಸಿಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಸಂಜಯನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದೇವತೆಗಳು ವೈಕುಂಠನೆಂದೂ ವೇದಗಳು ವಿಷ್ಣುವೆಂದೂ ಕರೆಯುವ ನಾರಾಯಣನ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಮುಗಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"संजय रमणक, हैरण्यवत, हरिवर्ष आदि वर्षों को उनके पर्वतों और निवासियों सहित गिनाते हैं। अन्त में वे उस नारायण का उल्लेख करते हैं जिन्हें देवता वैकुण्ठ और वेद विष्णु कहते हैं।","te":"రమణకం, హైరణ్యవతం, హరివర్షం మొదలైన వర్షాలను వాటి పర్వతాలు, నివాసులతో సంజయుడు చెబుతాడు. దేవతలు వైకుంఠుడని, వేదాలు విష్ణువని పిలిచే నారాయణుని ప్రస్తావనతో ముగిస్తాడు.","ta":"ரமணகம், ஹைரண்யவதம், ஹரிவர்ஷம் முதலிய வர்ஷங்களை அவற்றின் மலைகள், மக்களுடன் சஞ்சயன் பெயரிடுகிறான். தேவர்கள் வைகுண்டன் என்றும் வேதங்கள் விஷ்ணு என்றும் அழைக்கும் நாராயணனைக் குறிப்பிட்டு முடிக்கிறான்.","ml":"രമണകം, ഹൈരണ്യവതം, ഹരിവർഷം തുടങ്ങിയ വർഷങ്ങളെയും അവയുടെ പർവതങ്ങളെയും നിവാസികളെയും സഞ്ജയൻ പേരെടുത്ത് പറയുന്നു. ദേവന്മാർ വൈകുണ്ഠം എന്നും വേദങ്ങൾ വിഷ്ണു എന്നും വിളിക്കുന്ന നാരായണനെക്കുറിച്ചു പറഞ്ഞ് അദ്ദേഹം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.9; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"जम्बूखण्डविनिर्माणपर्व","titleEn":"Jambukhandavinirmana Parva (Description of Jambudvipa)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"वर्षाणां चैव नामानि पर्वतानां च संजय ।\nआचक्ष्व मे यथातत्त्वं ये च पर्वतवासिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, tell me truly the names of the regions and of the mountains, and of those who live on the mountains."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"दक्षिणेन तु श्वेतस्य नीलस्यैवोत्तरेण तु ।\nवर्षं रमणकं नाम जायन्ते तत्र मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"South of Shveta and north of Nila lies the region called Ramanaka, where human beings are born."}},{"n":3,"text":"शुक्लाभिजनसंपन्नाः सर्वे सुप्रियदर्शनाः ।\nरतिप्रधानाश्च तथा जायन्ते तत्र मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the people born there are of fair descent and very pleasing to see, and devoted chiefly to pleasure."}},{"n":4,"text":"दश वर्षसहस्राणि शतानि दश पञ्च च ।\nजीवन्ति ते महाराज नित्यं मुदितमानसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, they live eleven thousand years and five hundred, always cheerful."}},{"n":5,"text":"दक्षिणे शृङ्गिणश्चैव श्वेतस्याथोत्तरेण च ।\nवर्षं हैरण्वतं नाम यत्र हैरण्वती नदी ॥","meaning":{"en":"South of Shringin and north of Shveta lies the region called Hairanvata, where the river Hairanvati flows."}},{"n":6,"text":"यक्षानुगा महाराज धनिनः प्रियदर्शनाः ।\nमहाबलास्तत्र सदा राजन्मुदितमानसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, the people there are followers of the Yakshas, wealthy, pleasing to see and very strong, always glad at heart."}},{"n":7,"text":"एकादश सहस्राणि वर्षाणां ते जनाधिप ।\nआयुष्प्रमाणं जीवन्ति शतानि दश पञ्च च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the people, they live a span of eleven thousand years and five hundred."}},{"n":8,"text":"शृङ्गाणि वै शृङ्गवतस्त्रीण्येव मनुजाधिप ।\nएकं मणिमयं तत्र तथैकं रौक्ममद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shringavan has three peaks, lord of men: one is made of gems, one of wondrous gold, and one of all jewels, adorned with palaces."}},{"n":9,"text":"सर्वरत्नमयं चैकं भवनैरुपशोभितम् ।\nतत्र स्वयंप्रभा देवी नित्यं वसति शाण्डिली ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the goddess Shandili, self-luminous, always dwells."}},{"n":10,"text":"उत्तरेण तु शृङ्गस्य समुद्रान्ते जनाधिप ।\nवर्षमैरावतं नाम तस्माच्छृङ्गवतः परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"North of the peak, at the edge of the sea, lord of the people, lies the region called Airavata, beyond Shringavan."}},{"n":11,"text":"न तत्र सूर्यस्तपति न ते जीर्यन्ति मानवाः ।\nचन्द्रमाश्च सनक्षत्रो ज्योतिर्भूत इवावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sun does not burn there and the people do not age; the moon with its stars seems to be wrapped in light."}},{"n":12,"text":"पद्मप्रभाः पद्मवर्णाः पद्मपत्रनिभेक्षणाः ।\nपद्मपत्रसुगन्धाश्च जायन्ते तत्र मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"People there are born with the glow of lotuses, the colour of lotuses, eyes like lotus petals and the fragrance of lotus petals."}},{"n":13,"text":"अनिष्पन्दाः सुगन्धाश्च निराहारा जितेन्द्रियाः ।\nदेवलोकच्युताः सर्वे तथा विरजसो नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are free of sweat, fragrant, need no food and have mastered their senses; all have fallen from the world of the gods, and are free of passion, King."}},{"n":14,"text":"त्रयोदश सहस्राणि वर्षाणां ते जनाधिप ।\nआयुष्प्रमाणं जीवन्ति नरा भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the people, those people live thirteen thousand years, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":15,"text":"क्षीरोदस्य समुद्रस्य तथैवोत्तरतः प्रभुः ।\nहरिर्वसति वैकुण्ठः शकटे कनकात्मके ॥","meaning":{"en":"North of the Ocean of Milk, the Lord Hari Vaikuntha dwells in a golden cart."}},{"n":16,"text":"अष्टचक्रं हि तद्यानं भूतयुक्तं मनोजवम् ।\nअग्निवर्णं महावेगं जाम्बूनदपरिष्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That vehicle has eight wheels, is yoked with spirits, is swift as thought, fiery in colour, very fast and adorned with Jambunada gold."}},{"n":17,"text":"स प्रभुः सर्वभूतानां विभुश्च भरतर्षभ ।\nसंक्षेपो विस्तरश्चैव कर्ता कारयिता च सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He, the lord of all beings and all-pervading, best of the Bharatas, is brevity and expansion, the doer and the cause of doing."}},{"n":18,"text":"पृथिव्यापस्तथाकाशं वायुस्तेजश्च पार्थिव ।\nस यज्ञः सर्वभूतानामास्यं तस्य हुताशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, he is earth, water, space, air and fire; he is the sacrifice of all beings, and fire is his mouth."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"एवमुक्तः संजयेन धृतराष्ट्रो महामनाः ।\nध्यानमन्वगमद्राजा पुत्रान्प्रति जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by Sanjaya, the high-minded Dhritarashtra, lord of the people, fell into thought about his sons."}},{"n":20,"text":"स विचिन्त्य महाराज पुनरेवाब्रवीद्वचः ।\nअसंशयं सूतपुत्र कालः संक्षिपते जगत् ।\nसृजते च पुनः सर्वं नेह विद्यति शाश्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After reflecting, great king, he spoke again: \"Without doubt, son of the charioteer, Time draws in the world, and creates everything again; nothing here is eternal.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"नरो नारायणश्चैव सर्वज्ञः सर्वभूतभृत् ।\nदेवा वैकुण्ठ इत्याहुर्वेदा विष्णुरिति प्रभुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Nara and Narayana, the all-knowing sustainers of all beings, are called Vaikuntha by the gods, and the Vedas call the Lord Vishnu.\""}}]}]}